webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7791929Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7803036Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7907498Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7918485Z ^[[0m
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7919234Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7919798Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7920072Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7920817Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7921399Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7921758Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7921996Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7922453Z    if you are ready to continue.
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7922650Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7923118Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7924121Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7925193Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7925580Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7925785Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7926049Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7926324Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7926540Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7926947Z    can use Nix.
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7927118Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7927243Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7927423Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7927771Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7928266Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7934477Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7934727Z I will:
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7935051Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7935298Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7936034Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7936800Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7937323Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7937635Z  - install Nix in /nix
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7937934Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7938363Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7938772Z    /root
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7951267Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7952108Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7962937Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7963944Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7964639Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7965447Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7966139Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7983944Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7995419Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7996513Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7997489Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7998258Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7998645Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7998955Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7999435Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.7999803Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.8000522Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.8000926Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.8001051Z If you would like to
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.8001328Z see the output, try like this:
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:35:25.8001523Z 
